# - Deezer, Yu Mei artist page (opened 2026-10-20, https://www.deezer.com/artist/107130122): singles discography with dates, durations and writer credits. Eat Up 13 Jul 2020, Pine Up 19 Sep 2020, Dife Kako 9 Nov 2021, Leakey 14 Jan 2022, Youpi Ya (feat. Anonymous G) 29 Mar 2023, Pine Up (feat. Lambi) 29 Apr 2023, X 3 Apr 2024, 10 sur 10 24 Apr 2024, Laisse moi passer with Team Bwe Tou Sa 31 Oct 2024, PLAN A 3 (Femmes Fatales Edition Bouyon) 7 Sep 2024. Writer on nearly every title: Emmanuelle Titine. Also writing credits on SHAKE iT! by Shani Da Flava (3 Sep 2025, SIDESHOW) and on 7 sur 7 by Ricky Bishop on the #newbouyonexperience project (25 May 2025, Jeunes Visionnaires).
# - Shazam, PLAN A 3 (feat. Yu Mei) [Femmes Fatales Edition Bouyon], Yellow Gaza and Yumei (opened 2026-10-20): released September 7, 2024, label Vadore Concept Groupe, language French, BPM 157; performers Yellow Gaza and Yumei; composer Meyapin Bordin Allan; songwriters Letin Sylvia, Letin Severine and Titine Emmanuelle.
# - Shazam, Leakey by Yu Mei (opened 2026-10-20): released January 14, 2022 by Up World, BPM 146; performing artist credit Emmanuelle Titine, vocals; songwriters Brandon Benoist and Emmanuelle Titine; producer Jordan Sapotille.
# - Shazam, Pine Up (feat. Lambi) by Yu Mei (opened 2026-10-20): published lyrics in Antillean Creole mixed with French; page published date 2020-09-19 for the original Pine Up.
# - YouTube, T-BTS ft YU MEI, Laisse-moi passer, official clip description (opened 2026-10-20): presented as New Bouyon 2021, produced by CamRich, mastering GAMMALAB and Fly Beu Records, video by Dylan Farah, hashtags include UltimesPetasse and UPCREW; a photo credit is printed under the name YUMEI.UP. Cited as a clip credit only, not as a verified official account.
# - Faya podcast, Voicenotes from Guadeloupe: le bouyon episode (opened 2026-10-20 via Podtail): Renaud Brizard lands in Pointe-a-Pitre, Guadeloupe; guests include Yu Mei of Ultimes Petasses; published tracklist closes with Ultimes Petasses and Yu Mei, Eat Up, T-BTS and Yu Mei, Laisse-moi passer, and Ultimes Petasses and Yu Mei, Pine Up.
# - Le Mwakast, Acast feed (search result and feed, 2026-10-20): episode of May 23, 2023 titled YUMEI: Ultime P*tasse, presenting her as a bouyon singer, in a podcast devoted to Antillean culture.
# - France-Antilles interview republished by French Caribbean News, October 5, 2026 (opened 2026-10-20): Yu Mei, bouyon singer aged 29, speaks publicly after intimate videos of her were shared without her consent; she states she reported the facts to the competent authorities, refuses shame and refuses to let the case define her. Handled here briefly and factually, in her own stated terms.
# Note: no verified birthplace, no album and no verified official social account were found during this research, so none is printed. The Deezer artist page above was opened and verified, so it is the single sameAs link.

